-- ENVIRONMENTAL GATE LIMITATION (runner capability / pre-existing, NOT this surface) --
Full-app `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync[-macOS] build test` is the macOS-CI step
(p4-apple/P99 apple-acceptance-gate, macos-latest). On this shared CLT-default host it
is blocked by the SAME pre-existing, unrelated issues already tracked in
apps/macos-pending-verifications.md for every P4-apple surface:
  • the KMP `Shared.xcframework` is not staged (Frameworks/Shared.xcframework = .gitkeep;
    requires the Kotlin/Native Apple toolchain via the scheme's gradle pre-action),
  • `public struct DashboardWidgetSize` (+ PowerFlowConnection) redefined ~15× across
    Sources/DashboardWidgets/* + TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/*,
  • 150+ co-located *.Tests.swift import XCTest into the app target,
  • macOS app/widget targets need a development signing identity.
ZERO of these involve Features/Battery. The surface itself is proven green by the real
macOS SDK type-check, the SwiftPM release build, and the 30/30 XCTest run above (all via
the present Xcode 26.5 toolchain). This deferral is recorded in
apps/macos-pending-verifications.md.
GATE_ENV_BLOCKED=shared-xcframework-unstaged; dashboardwidgetsize-redef×15;
